<% content_for :title, "Registry — Shadwire" %>
<% content_for :description, "The static registry the CLI installs from: index.json, one JSON file per component with its source inside, and how to host your own." %>
<% content_for :head do %>
  <%= tag.style rouge_stylesheet %>
<% end %>

<article class="space-y-12">
  <%= render "docs/header",
        title: "Registry",
        description: "The CLI installs components from a set of static JSON files. There is no application server and no login." %>

  <section class="space-y-4">
    <p class="leading-7">
      Shadwire's registry is published at
      <%= link_to "shadwire.edumoraes.dev.br/r", "https://shadwire.edumoraes.dev.br/r/index.json", target: "_blank", rel: "noopener", class: "font-medium underline underline-offset-4" %>.
      It has an index with the catalog, and one file per item that contains the full source of
      each of the item's files.
    </p>

    <%= render "docs/table",
          headers: [ "URL", "Contents" ],
          rows: [
            [ docs_code("/r/index.json"), safe_join([ "The catalog (name, title, description, when to use) and ", docs_code("base"), ": the shared files and gems that init installs." ]) ],
            [ docs_code("/r/{name}.json"), "One component: its metadata, the other items it depends on, its API, and its files with their contents." ],
            [ docs_code("/r/llms.txt"), "The same catalog in plain text, for agents." ],
            [ docs_code("/r/llms-full.txt"), "Every component's full API in plain text." ]
          ] %>

    <%= docs_code_block(@snippets[:fetch], language: :shell) %>
  </section>

  <section class="space-y-4">
    <%= docs_h2("index.json") %>
    <p class="leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
      <%= docs_code("list") %> and <%= docs_code("search") %> read this file, and
      <%= docs_code("init") %> gets the base files from it.
    </p>

    <%= docs_code_block(@snippets[:index], language: :json) %>
  </section>

  <section class="space-y-4">
    <%= docs_h2("One item") %>
    <p class="leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
      Each item has everything needed to install it in a single request, file contents
      included. <%= docs_code("registryDependencies") %> already includes the dependencies of
      dependencies, so the CLI does not have to look them up one by one.
    </p>

    <%= docs_code_block(@snippets[:item], language: :json) %>

    <%= render "docs/table",
          headers: [ "Field", "What it is" ],
          rows: [
            [ docs_code("whenToUse"), "A sentence on when to use this component and which similar ones to consider. Search matches against this text." ],
            [ docs_code("usage"), "ERB snippets for the most common uses." ],
            [ docs_code("registryDependencies"), "The other items that get installed with it, including indirect dependencies." ],
            [ docs_code("requiresStimulus"), "True when the item installs a controller under app/javascript/." ],
            [ docs_code("api.components[]"), "Read from the source code: class, helper, variants, sizes, arguments and attributes." ],
            [ docs_code("files[]"), safe_join([ "Each file as ", docs_code("{ target, type, content }"), ". Paths inside the Shadwire repository are left out." ]) ]
          ] %>
  </section>

  <section class="space-y-4">
    <%= docs_h2("How it is built") %>
    <p class="leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
      It starts from <%= docs_code("registry/registry.json") %> in the Shadwire repository,
      which lists each item's files as <%= docs_code("source") %> → <%= docs_code("target") %>
      pairs. <%= docs_code("bin/build_registry") %> turns that into the published registry: it
      copies in each file's contents and reads the API from the source:
    </p>

    <%= docs_code_block(@snippets[:build], language: :shell) %>

    <p class="leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
      The output goes to <%= docs_code("build/") %>, which is generated and should not be
      edited by hand. CI rebuilds it on every push to <%= docs_code("main") %>, when it deploys
      this site.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="space-y-4">
    <%= docs_h2("Serving your own") %>
    <p class="leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
      These are static files, so you can host them anywhere: a storage bucket, GitHub Pages,
      a directory behind a web server. Point the CLI at it with <%= docs_code("--registry") %>,
      or pass the flag to <%= docs_code("init") %> to save it in
      <%= docs_code("shadwire.json") %>.
    </p>

    <p class="leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
      <%= docs_code("file://") %> URLs work too, which is handy for testing a registry you
      built locally:
    </p>

    <%= docs_code_block(@snippets[:local], language: :shell) %>

    <%= render layout: "docs/callout", locals: { icon: "triangle-alert", title: "The registry URL is written into the user's app" } do %>
      <code>shadwire.json</code> keeps the URL that was used when <code>init</code> ran. Apps
      that already installed from you keep using that address, so if you move a registry,
      leave a redirect at the old URL.
    <% end %>
  </section>
</article>
